# Core Principles

- Minimize scope: smallest correct diff wins.
- Reuse before create: search the codebase before writing new code.
- Validate conclusions with evidence: grep, tests, lints — not assumptions.
- Before non-trivial work: pre-code gate (or sparc-lite for large features); read project ADRs/rules.
- After proven success: run auto-skill-mint criteria; mint `gen-*` only if all pass.
- When applying a `gen-*` skill: bump `x-use-count` and `x-last-used` (best effort).
- Project-specific decisions belong in project ADRs, not global gen skills.
